1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 1)

3
00:01:27,359 --> 00:01:28,359
Boss P'Eng.

4
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:30,799
These cigarettes seem a bit damp.

5
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,399
I've already had someone
fetch a fresh pack.

6
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,480
They'll be here any second.

7
00:01:33,879 --> 00:01:35,680
This pack was kept with Xiaofang.

8
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:38,096
Last time, because the
drink he mixed was too fizzy,

9
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,680
didn't you pour it over his head?

10
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,120
They probably got splashed.

11
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,760
Are these the candidates
for Boss P'Eng to review?

12
00:02:05,079 --> 00:02:06,079
Yes.

13
00:02:06,439 --> 00:02:07,439
Yeah.

14
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,160
Here are Boss P'Eng's cigarettes.

15
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,680
Hold on a second.

16
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,440
Boss P'Eng wants you to light it.

17
00:02:25,759 --> 00:02:26,759
Me?

18
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,400
Boss P'Eng.

19
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,400
Boss P'Eng.

20
00:02:37,152 --> 00:02:38,152
Allow me.

21
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:57,960
Boss P'Eng.

22
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:21,280
Who gave you permission to
tie that red bandana on him?

23
00:03:21,919 --> 00:03:22,919
I...

24
00:03:23,439 --> 00:03:25,159
Didn't Taozi always wear one?

25
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:27,520
I figured Boss P'Eng was into that look.

26
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,999
This kid sure got lucky.

27
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,879
It's hard to say if it's
a blessing or a curse.

28
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:42,159
Come here.

29
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,080
Take it off.

30
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,280
And that too.

31
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,240
Open your mouth.

32
00:04:28,839 --> 00:04:29,879
B-Boss P'Eng.

33
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,600
What did you say?

34
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:39,920
I told you...

35
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,480
open your mouth.

36
00:04:59,759 --> 00:05:01,759
You think you're worthy
of dressing like this?

37
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,240
Wow.

38
00:06:19,759 --> 00:06:20,240
A Pong.

39
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,199
This is ready, take it out.

40
00:06:25,097 --> 00:06:26,017
Don't start.

41
00:06:26,041 --> 00:06:27,559
The girl from Huabo who just ordered...

42
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,120
took a call and vanished into thin air.

43
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,360
Oh, she ordered but isn't eating?

44
00:06:33,399 --> 00:06:34,920
She's here chasing celebrities.

45
00:06:35,199 --> 00:06:36,999
Said some big star from Huabo...

46
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,240
is coming here to shoot a show.

47
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,599
She answered a call...

48
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,398
and dashed out like she won the lottery.

49
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:43,479
Isn't that wild?

50
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,720
Hey, she's actually from my hometown.

51
00:06:46,079 --> 00:06:47,638
She already paid for this fried rice.

52
00:06:47,639 --> 00:06:48,639
Said it's on her.

53
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,920
I just can't understand how
crazy fans are these days.

54
00:06:52,439 --> 00:06:53,639
Well, that's great.

55
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,800
We can bring it over
for Xiaotong and Xiaoya.

56
00:06:57,199 --> 00:06:58,399
Let's just eat it ourselves.

57
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,240
A Pong.

58
00:07:01,399 --> 00:07:03,536
There's a celebrity coming
to the night market tonight.

59
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,278
It's going to be packed with people.

60
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:07,439
Xiaotong and Xiaoya will
probably be exhausted.

61
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,920
How about this? If you want some,

62
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,559
I can save half for you, okay?

63
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,120
It's fine.

64
00:07:13,121 --> 00:07:14,198
I'm not that hungry.

65
00:07:14,199 --> 00:07:15,199
Let the kids have it all.

66
00:07:15,319 --> 00:07:18,529
Let them eat their fill so they'll have
the energy to help us draw in customers.

67
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,520
We're definitely going
to make a killing tonight.

68
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,119
Why was the shoot moved up?

69
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,320
Wasn't it scheduled for eight?

70
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:30,359
The production crew was worried
about too many fans gathering...

71
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,240
and causing a riot.

72
00:07:31,241 --> 00:07:32,519
So they started early.

73
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,199
That guy's outfit today...

74
00:07:38,519 --> 00:07:39,680
Did you approve it?

75
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,920
It was my negligence.

76
00:07:41,439 --> 00:07:42,679
I didn't check thoroughly beforehand.

77
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:44,160
I'm willing to accept any punishment.

78
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,839
You should know my
rules better than anyone.

79
00:07:48,319 --> 00:07:49,878
Anyone who tries to imitate his look...

80
00:07:49,879 --> 00:07:51,079
and appears in front of me...

81
00:07:52,319 --> 00:07:53,480
has a death wish.

82
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,160
There won't be a next time.

83
00:07:57,161 --> 00:07:58,576
There absolutely won't be a next time.

84
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,016
I'll write a formal apology
as soon as I get back.

85
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,120
And reflect on my mistakes.

86
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,399
That boy...

87
00:08:06,879 --> 00:08:07,879
send him to the hospital.

88
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,680
I'll cover the expenses.

89
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:44,158
Excuse me.

90
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:45,199
Excuse me, coming through.

91
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,240
Excuse me, coming through.

92
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,039
Please make way.

93
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,039
Thank you.

94
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:49,720
Please make way.

95
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:50,720
Thanks.

96
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,639
Coming through.

97
00:08:53,759 --> 00:08:54,759
Excuse me, coming through.

98
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:55,918
Excuse me.

99
00:08:55,919 --> 00:08:56,840
A Pong.

100
00:08:56,919 --> 00:08:58,119
There are so many people today.

101
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,120
Yeah.

102
00:09:00,159 --> 00:09:01,319
Excuse me, coming through.

103
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,320
Excuse me.

104
00:09:19,879 --> 00:09:21,399
I wonder how business is doing.

105
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,280
Looks like they're selling well.

106
00:09:25,159 --> 00:09:26,039
Xiaotong.

107
00:09:26,159 --> 00:09:26,960
Brother!

108
00:09:26,961 --> 00:09:28,038
Brother A Pong!

109
00:09:28,039 --> 00:09:29,119
How are sales?

110
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,120
Good.

111
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,440
Thank you.

112
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,079
How are sales going today?

113
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,080
Xiaoya.

114
00:09:35,559 --> 00:09:36,200
Brother!

115
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,080
There's a huge crowd today.

116
00:09:37,081 --> 00:09:38,239
The flowers are almost sold out.

117
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,158
That's amazing! You
haven't eaten yet, right?

118
00:09:40,159 --> 00:09:41,296
You and your sister go eat first.

119
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,360
I'll clean up the rest.

120
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:49,960
Come have a taste.

121
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:53,320
Egg fried rice.

122
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:55,960
Thanks, brother!

123
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,960
Mmhmm.

124
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,599
Wow, egg fried rice!

125
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,000
It's been so long since I had this.

126
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,720
A Pong.

127
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,080
You can't sell this stuff here.

128
00:10:09,519 --> 00:10:10,240
It's fine.

129
00:10:10,241 --> 00:10:11,881
The cops won't come around here at night.

130
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,399
Careful, young master.

131
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,120
This way.

132
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,558
Excuse me, coming through.

133
00:10:54,559 --> 00:10:55,720
Excuse me, coming through.

134
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,440
Excuse me.

135
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,679
Coming through.

136
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:03,600
Right here.

137
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,840
What is it, young master?

138
00:11:06,039 --> 00:11:07,439
Are you sure we should go this way?

139
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:08,799
Yes, young master.

140
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,456
The road ahead is completely
blocked by fans and the crowd.

141
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,559
This is the only shortcut.

142
00:11:18,039 --> 00:11:19,080
This way, young master.

143
00:11:27,759 --> 00:11:28,240
Are you okay?

144
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:28,840
What are you doing?

145
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:29,360
Get up.

146
00:11:29,361 --> 00:11:30,761
Take it easy, everything fell over.

147
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:31,960
Be careful.

148
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,000
Are you okay?

149
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,320
Go to the back for now.

150
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,918
Hello.

151
00:11:37,919 --> 00:11:39,080
Do you remember me?

152
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,798
You're the fried rice
girl from my hometown.

153
00:11:40,799 --> 00:11:41,679
Right.

154
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:42,559
I'm so sorry.

155
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,879
We didn't notice.

156
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,558
How about you tell us how
much these flowers cost?

157
00:11:45,559 --> 00:11:46,759
We'll compensate you for them.

158
00:11:47,279 --> 00:11:48,440
A Pong, what's going on?

159
00:11:48,519 --> 00:11:50,758
This is the hometown girl with
the fried rice I mentioned today.

160
00:11:50,759 --> 00:11:51,320
Hello.

161
00:11:51,321 --> 00:11:53,960
And she said she wants
to pay for all these flowers.

162
00:11:54,159 --> 00:11:55,159
Yeah.

163
00:11:55,399 --> 00:11:56,399
It's no big deal.

164
00:11:57,399 --> 00:11:59,518
These flowers were just leftovers anyway.

165
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:00,798
They're not worth much anyway.

166
00:12:00,799 --> 00:12:02,840
Besides, didn't you treat us to fried rice?

167
00:12:04,679 --> 00:12:06,119
He says you don't need
to pay for the flowers.

168
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:06,799
Yeah.

169
00:12:06,799 --> 00:12:07,759
Welcome to Tailan.

170
00:12:07,759 --> 00:12:08,759
Yeah.

171
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:11,199
And thanks again for treating
us to the egg fried rice earlier.

172
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,439
We couldn't possibly do that.

173
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,240
Let's pool our money and pay you back.

174
00:12:18,559 --> 00:12:19,559
How about this?

175
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:21,480
You guys buy all these flowers.

176
00:12:21,679 --> 00:12:22,679
We'll give you a discount.

177
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,359
Later, when your idol
finishes shooting the show,

178
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,398
I'll help you give them to him.

179
00:12:25,399 --> 00:12:26,200
I know the security guard.

180
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:26,600
Really?

181
00:12:26,601 --> 00:12:27,719
You know the security guard?

182
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:28,480
Sure.

183
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,480
Sounds good!

184
00:12:30,279 --> 00:12:30,679
I really didn't expect...

185
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:32,600
- They're actually buying them?
- They're really buying them.

186
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:33,559
Come on, kids.

187
00:12:33,559 --> 00:12:34,120
We've got work to do.

188
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,120
Wrap the flowers up nicely.

189
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:36,000
We've got big clients!

190
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Okay!

191
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,039
We'll take all the pink ones.

192
00:12:39,399 --> 00:12:40,480
Sure, you got it!

193
00:12:41,039 --> 00:12:41,559
Look.

194
00:12:41,679 --> 00:12:42,120
Okay.

195
00:12:42,279 --> 00:12:43,839
Look, that one in the back is nice too.

196
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,200
Here.

197
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,240
Our homemade grape juice.

198
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:47,600
Thank you.

199
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:47,879
Have a taste.

200
00:12:47,879 --> 00:12:48,200
Thanks.

201
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,200
Thanks.

202
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:53,240
How is it?

203
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:53,679
Tastes good, right?

204
00:12:53,679 --> 00:12:54,399
It's so good!

205
00:12:54,399 --> 00:12:55,399
Of course.

206
00:12:55,552 --> 00:12:58,488
Young Master, I'll call the production
team to send someone to pick us up.

207
00:12:58,519 --> 00:12:59,519
Yeah.

208
00:13:04,159 --> 00:13:05,960
Is that the star you like?

209
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,159
Yes.

210
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:08,720
I'm actually a bit shy about it.

211
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:10,200
Can I take a look?

212
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,000
Sure.

213
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:11,559
Here.

214
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:14,038
Just how handsome is he for you
to chase him all the way to Tailan?

215
00:13:14,039 --> 00:13:15,039
Take a look.

216
00:13:18,833 --> 00:13:19,833
What do you think?

217
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:21,960
Isn't he handsome?

218
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,479
He is.

219
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,200
Keep it safe.

220
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:25,879
Don't lose it.

221
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:26,480
You've got good taste.

222
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:27,839
Later, when he performs,

223
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,360
how are you planning to cheer for him?

224
00:13:29,616 --> 00:13:31,655
We'll just give him this bouquet.

225
00:13:31,679 --> 00:13:33,639
It'd be great if you
bought a lottery ticket too.

226
00:13:33,679 --> 00:13:35,079
Giving flowers is more romantic.

227
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,000
Don't you get it?

228
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
He likes flowers.

229
00:13:37,639 --> 00:13:39,439
Why don't you buy
the lottery ticket as well?

230
00:13:39,759 --> 00:13:41,919
You can give him a
lottery rose along with it.

231
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:15,960
Hey, look over here!

232
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:28,080
Are you okay?

233
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,519
Are you alright?

234
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:31,519
Get up, quick.

235
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,644
I'm talking to you, can't
you even say thank you?

236
00:14:34,668 --> 00:14:37,148
Mingkun, Mingkun!

237
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,440
Young Master.

238
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,440
What happened to you?

239
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:44,720
What the hell are you doing?

240
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,159
A Pong.

241
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,200
Hurry.

242
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:46,799
I'm so sorry.

243
00:14:46,799 --> 00:14:47,320
It's our fault.

244
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:47,799
Young Master.

245
00:14:47,799 --> 00:14:48,799
We are truly sorry.

246
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,159
Young Master.

247
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,959
The production team
has prepared new clothes.

248
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,159
Let's go change first.

249
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,200
This way.

250
00:14:59,159 --> 00:15:00,360
Break it up, everyone.

251
00:15:01,399 --> 00:15:02,440
I'm really sorry.

252
00:15:03,559 --> 00:15:04,638
Regarding compensation,

253
00:15:04,639 --> 00:15:06,239
I hope you can contact me proactively.

254
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,240
Here is the phone number.

255
00:15:07,639 --> 00:15:08,798
We are really sorry.

256
00:15:08,799 --> 00:15:10,720
We didn't expect this to happen either.

257
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:11,960
Yeah.

258
00:15:13,399 --> 00:15:14,679
What kind of person is that?

259
00:15:15,279 --> 00:15:17,518
I'd like to see which
entitled brat is so arrogant.

260
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:18,919
Yingyu Group...?

261
00:15:22,457 --> 00:15:23,217
Pao Bei.

262
00:15:23,241 --> 00:15:25,639
Isn't this the group your mom works for?

263
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:30,360
It seems to be the flower
nursery owned by the group's boss.

264
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:45,158
Let's welcome our brand friend from Huabo,

265
00:15:45,159 --> 00:15:46,559
Li Milan.

266
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,279
Hello, everyone.

267
00:15:59,279 --> 00:16:00,279
I'm Li Milan.

268
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,279
I'm very happy to meet you all in Tailan.

269
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:09,240
This is the new product
endorsed by Mr. Milan.

270
00:16:09,399 --> 00:16:11,399
Please give it your full support, okay?

271
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,720
This guy has changed a lot.

272
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,840
A Pong.

273
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:33,999
Here are the flowers you
wanted, all wrapped up.

274
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,600
They're definitely perfect for a star.

275
00:16:35,679 --> 00:16:36,679
How are you?

276
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,200
How are you feeling?

277
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:38,840
Are you okay?

278
00:16:38,841 --> 00:16:40,495
Are you sure you don't
need to go to the hospital?

279
00:16:40,519 --> 00:16:41,000
Look.

280
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
I'm perfectly fine.

281
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:43,720
But what's up with you?

282
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,359
Why did you lose your
temper like that just now?

283
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,600
You scared Xiaotong and Xiaoya.

284
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,480
You know I hate rich
snobs who love to show off.

285
00:16:49,679 --> 00:16:51,360
He was clearly the one bullying us.

286
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:52,559
Why blame us?

287
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:54,280
I haven't even mentioned how he held us up.

288
00:16:56,559 --> 00:16:58,239
You've got a grudge against the rich, huh?

289
00:16:59,759 --> 00:17:01,239
It's not like I haven't told you before.

290
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,440
I do hate the rich.

291
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,575
They were born with a
silver spoon in their mouths,

292
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:07,199
while we have to roll around in the mud.

293
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,558
What we bust our asses to earn in a year

294
00:17:08,559 --> 00:17:10,176
isn't even as much as they spend in a day.

295
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:12,239
But there's nothing we
can do about it, right?

296
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,480
Everyone has their own destiny.

297
00:17:15,976 --> 00:17:17,236
Wow, he's even making a heart sign.

298
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:19,640
He's so handsome!

299
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,240
No wonder he has so many fans.

300
00:17:23,759 --> 00:17:25,559
How is he handsome?

301
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,759
If we put on his styling and clothes,

302
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,400
wouldn't we look way better than him?

303
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,680
He's obviously very handsome.

304
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,920
Look.

305
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,879
Mr. Milan prefers eating this,

306
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,799
so please buy more of it, okay?

307
00:17:39,039 --> 00:17:40,039
Okay!

308
00:17:41,839 --> 00:17:43,960
He was super sloppy in college.

309
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,656
He didn't even wash his clothes.

310
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,159
Oh, really?

311
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:49,640
Did you know him before?

312
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,880
Haven't I told you before?

313
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:55,200
He was that annoying deskmate I had in college.

314
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,358
You mean the one...

315
00:17:58,359 --> 00:17:58,839
Yes.

316
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,798
The one who always
competed with you in college,

317
00:18:00,799 --> 00:18:01,999
the one who always bullied you?

318
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
That's him.

319
00:18:03,079 --> 00:18:04,119
So it was him!

320
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,160
Exactly.

321
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,440
He's just a jerk.

322
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,840
To bump into him even here...

323
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,240
It's a small world for enemies.

324
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,359
Hey, who knows?

325
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,279
Maybe your meeting this time

326
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:20,119
will kick off a brand new romance.

327
00:18:21,839 --> 00:18:24,919
Next, please welcome the
boss of our Yingyu brand,

328
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:27,000
the handsome Boss P'Eng!

329
00:18:43,279 --> 00:18:44,279
Hello, everyone.

330
00:18:44,319 --> 00:18:47,359
I'm the CEO of Yingyu Group,

331
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:48,359
and also your good friend,

332
00:18:48,359 --> 00:18:49,119
Junying.

333
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,359
So handsome!

334
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:52,399
Thank you all for your
support and for coming.

335
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:53,400
Thank you.

336
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,279
Who's your friend?

337
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,439
He was just glaring at us fiercely,

338
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,216
and now he's pretending
to be a man of the people.

339
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:00,240
Bah!

340
00:19:01,559 --> 00:19:04,319
That's why he gets to be the big boss.

341
00:19:04,519 --> 00:19:06,039
He knows exactly what to say to whom.

342
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:07,359
What did you expect?

343
00:19:07,559 --> 00:19:09,680
Isn't he just like our restaurant boss?

344
00:19:09,799 --> 00:19:11,239
All smiles to the customers,

345
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,400
but bossing us around.

346
00:19:13,079 --> 00:19:16,000
Look at him dressed like a flashy peacock.

347
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,839
You'd think he was making
his center debut today.

348
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,799
Alright.

349
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:25,359
Isn't that the guy who
fell by the road earlier?

350
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,318
Is he a star here in Tailan?

351
00:19:27,319 --> 00:19:28,200
He's so handsome!

352
00:19:28,201 --> 00:19:30,319
He's just a boss who sells soy sauce.

353
00:19:32,079 --> 00:19:33,518
He's just a boss?

354
00:19:33,519 --> 00:19:35,159
He really has that star aura.

355
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:36,919
Are you ditching your precious Xiaolan?

356
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:38,416
Becoming a fan of someone else so quickly?

357
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,839
How is that possible?

358
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:43,119
I've liked Xiaolan for five years.

359
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:47,000
It hasn't been easy
for him since his debut.

360
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:49,120
How could I easily switch
to liking someone else?

361
00:19:50,759 --> 00:19:52,679
It brings tears to my
eyes just thinking about it.

362
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:54,440
How hard could it possibly be for him?

363
00:19:55,359 --> 00:19:56,919
If I really had to go into detail,

364
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:58,759
it would take hours to finish the story.

365
00:20:00,079 --> 00:20:02,599
He debuted on his company's
group formation night.

366
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,159
Actually, during the
previous public performances,

367
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:06,599
he was always in first place.

368
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,200
But for some unknown reason,

369
00:20:08,599 --> 00:20:11,119
he ended up in last
place during the finals.

370
00:20:11,559 --> 00:20:13,440
There are six people in their group, right?

371
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:16,240
So they started calling
him the eternal sixth place.

372
00:20:17,319 --> 00:20:19,200
Who knows who he managed to offend.

373
00:20:20,359 --> 00:20:22,920
This crappy company only
knows how to exploit him,

374
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:25,320
and doesn't care about him at all.

375
00:20:26,079 --> 00:20:27,758
But I'm really happy to see him today.

376
00:20:27,759 --> 00:20:29,119
Let's not talk about this anymore.

377
00:20:34,359 --> 00:20:35,598
It's fine.

378
00:20:35,599 --> 00:20:36,599
Your flowers.

379
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:38,119
Thank you.

380
00:20:38,119 --> 00:20:39,119
Go cheer for him!

381
00:20:43,799 --> 00:20:44,920
Milan really has it tough.

382
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:47,599
Three, two, one. It's available for purchase!

383
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:52,039
Please support our new product.

384
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,920
Milan!

385
00:20:57,056 --> 00:21:00,190
[The Yingyu Group's account livestreaming
with fans commenting that they love Milan]

386
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,679
Alright, besides the autographed photos,

387
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,159
we've also prepared

388
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:11,318
our limited edition
gift boxes for everyone.

389
00:21:11,319 --> 00:21:13,358
It includes a custom sauce spoon

390
00:21:13,359 --> 00:21:14,880
and a Milan standee.

391
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
The last one hundred orders!

392
00:21:16,001 --> 00:21:17,559
Three, two, one.

393
00:21:17,839 --> 00:21:18,839
The link is up!

394
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:26,680
A Pong.

395
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:27,559
Ah?

396
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:29,080
Aren't you going to charge for this?

397
00:21:29,359 --> 00:21:30,000
It's fine.

398
00:21:30,001 --> 00:21:31,015
No need to charge for this.

399
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,519
Later, when they're done,

400
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,799
we'll give the flowers to them for free.

401
00:21:35,039 --> 00:21:36,199
They'll think we're generous,

402
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,880
and then buy all the lottery tickets.

403
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:40,038
Isn't that killing two
birds with one stone?

404
00:21:40,039 --> 00:21:41,039
Yeah.

405
00:21:42,279 --> 00:21:43,279
Xiaotong, Xiaoya.

406
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:43,880
Yeah.

407
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:44,440
Here.

408
00:21:44,799 --> 00:21:46,480
Grab one each.

409
00:21:46,759 --> 00:21:47,759
Thanks, bro.

410
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:51,160
Xiaotong.

411
00:21:51,279 --> 00:21:52,400
Take Xiaoya home first.

412
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,480
It gets too chaotic here at night.

413
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,119
I can handle this myself.

414
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,839
Bro, you haven't eaten yet, right?

415
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,440
I'm fine.

416
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:58,680
You guys head home first.

417
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,119
Take good care of your sister.

418
00:22:00,119 --> 00:22:01,119
Got it.

419
00:22:04,079 --> 00:22:04,720
Let's go.

420
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:05,079
See ya.

421
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:06,440
Bye-bye.

422
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:21,400
Is this yours?

423
00:22:22,079 --> 00:22:23,160
Yes.

424
00:22:23,359 --> 00:22:24,440
We received a tip.

425
00:22:24,519 --> 00:22:26,359
That you're selling
lottery tickets illegally.

426
00:22:27,839 --> 00:22:29,279
No, Officer.

427
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:31,495
We're just ordinary citizens
doing a little business.

428
00:22:31,519 --> 00:22:32,519
How is that illegal?

429
00:22:35,279 --> 00:22:36,119
What are you doing?

430
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,240
What are you doing?

431
00:22:39,599 --> 00:22:40,758
A Pong, don't do anything rash.

432
00:22:40,759 --> 00:22:41,759
Calm down.

433
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:44,160
We're confiscating this for a few days.

434
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:47,000
You can pick it up at the station later.

435
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,160
Let's go.

436
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,480
They...

437
00:22:55,559 --> 00:22:56,798
Why would anyone report us?

438
00:22:56,799 --> 00:22:58,479
It must be that "Red Spider" from earlier.

439
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,680
Who's "Red Spider"?

440
00:23:01,359 --> 00:23:03,359
That flashy, unlucky boss.

441
00:23:03,759 --> 00:23:05,239
I can't think of anyone else but him.

442
00:23:05,279 --> 00:23:05,839
Let me tell you.

443
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,799
These capitalists are the most petty.

444
00:23:08,319 --> 00:23:09,639
They hold grudges over the smallest things.

445
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:10,758
If I catch him...

446
00:23:10,759 --> 00:23:11,919
I'll definitely make him pay.

447
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,439
Looks like they're wrapping up over there.

448
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:18,798
Milan doesn't seem to be coming this way.

449
00:23:18,799 --> 00:23:19,680
What do we do?

450
00:23:19,799 --> 00:23:21,079
Do you know which way he went?

451
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:24,240
I think it's that way.

452
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:25,160
Yeah.

453
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:26,160
That's the car.

454
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:27,319
Let's go.

455
00:23:27,319 --> 00:23:27,920
Hurry up.

456
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:28,400
Quick!

457
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,400
Go!

458
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:32,400
Excuse me.

459
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:33,640
Coming through.

460
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:34,519
Make way.

461
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:36,439
Roll down the window and take this!

462
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:38,038
These are flowers from your fans!

463
00:23:38,039 --> 00:23:39,039
Can you open the door?

464
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,440
Open the door!

465
00:23:40,519 --> 00:23:41,200
Roll down the window!

466
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:41,920
Open the door!

467
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:43,600
Just rolling down the window is fine too!

468
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,798
It's just a bouquet of flowers!

469
00:23:48,799 --> 00:23:49,920
Why so arrogant?

470
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:55,200
Hey, excuse me.

471
00:23:55,519 --> 00:23:56,519
Coming through.

472
00:23:57,039 --> 00:23:58,039
Hold this for me.

473
00:23:58,359 --> 00:23:59,656
I'm going to get revenge
on that soy sauce boss.

474
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:00,758
You shouldn't go.

475
00:24:00,759 --> 00:24:02,079
The car will drive off soon.

476
00:24:02,319 --> 00:24:02,680
A Pong!

477
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:03,119
It's fine.

478
00:24:03,359 --> 00:24:03,720
A Pong!

479
00:24:03,721 --> 00:24:05,401
Don't forget what your brother used to do.

480
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:08,640
He runs way too fast.

481
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:12,759
But I guess the flowers won't be delivered.

482
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:13,960
Give them to me.

483
00:24:14,039 --> 00:24:14,799
It's okay.

484
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:15,759
I'll deliver them for you.

485
00:24:15,759 --> 00:24:16,599
I promise they'll get there.

486
00:25:45,599 --> 00:25:46,599
You're stalking me.

487
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:48,960
I...

488
00:25:50,079 --> 00:25:51,599
I'm here to deliver flowers.

489
00:26:20,359 --> 00:26:21,640
Deliver flowers?

490
00:26:28,839 --> 00:26:29,839
What flowers?

491
00:26:30,279 --> 00:26:31,279
No.

492
00:26:31,319 --> 00:26:32,319
Never mind.

493
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:07,440
Are you messing with me?

494
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:11,400
What do you mean?

495
00:27:20,119 --> 00:27:22,240
Are you mocking me for being damaged goods?

496
00:27:26,319 --> 00:27:27,440
Is that it?

497
00:27:29,359 --> 00:27:30,359
No, it's not that!

498
00:27:30,559 --> 00:27:31,839
These aren't for you.

499
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,880
They're from fans for that celebrity.

500
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:36,480
Who knew you'd be the
one getting into that car?

501
00:27:37,119 --> 00:27:38,119
What's wrong?

502
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,480
Am I not worthy of sitting in that car?

503
00:27:40,599 --> 00:27:41,599
No.

504
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:44,599
These flowers aren't for me.

505
00:27:45,039 --> 00:27:46,559
You're trying to stalk me, aren't you?

506
00:27:51,559 --> 00:27:52,559
I thought...

507
00:27:53,279 --> 00:27:55,359
You were captivated by me earlier.

508
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:57,400
And decided to throw yourself at me.

509
00:27:57,960 --> 00:27:59,759
Haven't had enough yet?

510
00:28:02,759 --> 00:28:04,079
Kid.

511
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:10,936
You were the one who
slipped and fell earlier.

512
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:13,373
If we're really going to point
fingers, it has nothing to do with me.

513
00:28:17,519 --> 00:28:18,640
Was that food yours?

514
00:28:19,359 --> 00:28:20,599
Was that water yours too?

515
00:28:23,480 --> 00:28:24,758
Well, yes.

516
00:28:24,759 --> 00:28:26,799
Then how can you say it
has nothing to do with you?

517
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:31,559
Who else would it be?

518
00:28:36,359 --> 00:28:37,440
Or perhaps...

519
00:28:37,799 --> 00:28:38,960
You did it on purpose.

520
00:28:41,079 --> 00:28:43,960
To intentionally get my attention.

521
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:45,960
Huh?

522
00:28:48,039 --> 00:28:49,439
I apologize for my behavior earlier.

523
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:50,440
However,

524
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:51,559
I have things to do.

525
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:53,079
So I'll be taking off now.

526
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:56,960
What are you doing?

527
00:28:56,961 --> 00:28:58,001
What are you trying to do?

528
00:28:59,079 --> 00:29:00,079
Let go of me!

529
00:29:00,359 --> 00:29:00,839
It hurts!

530
00:29:00,839 --> 00:29:01,839
What do you want?

531
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:04,000
Stop it!

532
00:29:04,359 --> 00:29:05,359
Let me go!

533
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,119
Don't move.

534
00:29:09,599 --> 00:29:10,759
You dare mess with me?

535
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,240
You're dead meat.

536
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:16,240
What do I want to do?

537
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:18,200
You'll find out soon enough.

538
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,798
I have the right to personal freedom!

539
00:29:21,799 --> 00:29:22,880
This is kidnapping!

540
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:24,400
Believe it or not, I can sue you!

541
00:29:24,920 --> 00:29:25,920
Fine.

542
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,039
Go ahead and sue me.

543
00:29:52,559 --> 00:29:54,039
You're in quite a leisurely mood.

544
00:30:07,039 --> 00:30:08,039
Thank you.

545
00:30:09,160 --> 00:30:11,278
Boss P'Eng said you've been
standing for so long today.

546
00:30:11,279 --> 00:30:12,399
You must be exhausted.

547
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:14,880
So he wanted to treat you to a
Thai massage to help you relax.

548
00:30:15,519 --> 00:30:18,160
Master Chen here
exclusively serves Boss P'Eng.

549
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,838
His techniques are highly professional.

550
00:30:19,839 --> 00:30:20,839
Please enjoy yourself.

551
00:30:21,039 --> 00:30:22,399
Thank you for being so thoughtful.

552
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:23,400
You're too kind.

553
00:30:23,480 --> 00:30:25,038
Boss P'Eng also specifically
instructed me to say,

554
00:30:25,039 --> 00:30:26,798
he's especially grateful for
your live stream event this time.

555
00:30:26,799 --> 00:30:28,599
It brought us very impressive sales.

556
00:30:29,839 --> 00:30:31,775
It's mainly because your
company's products taste great.

557
00:30:31,799 --> 00:30:33,799
I tried a few new flavors
at the event earlier.

558
00:30:34,119 --> 00:30:35,119
They were all amazing.

559
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:38,416
By the way, these are the new
products we specially prepared for you.

560
00:30:38,440 --> 00:30:40,600
You can take them back
and enjoy them at your leisure.

561
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:41,839
Thank you so much.

562
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:43,799
It's been a pleasure working with you.

563
00:30:44,559 --> 00:30:45,759
Good evening, sir.

564
00:30:46,279 --> 00:30:47,518
Do you have a reservation?

565
00:30:47,519 --> 00:30:49,519
If not, we're currently fully booked.

566
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:51,880
Yes, I have a reservation.

567
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:52,400
I have one.

568
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:55,239
May I have the last name and
phone number for the reservation?

569
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:56,359
I'll look it up for you.

570
00:30:58,039 --> 00:30:59,319
Phone number...

571
00:31:03,119 --> 00:31:05,679
Sir, you can change your
clothes and take a shower first.

572
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,159
Master Chen will be here shortly.

573
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:09,279
You can rest for a bit after changing.

574
00:31:09,319 --> 00:31:10,319
Okay.

575
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:12,720
Mr. Milan.

576
00:31:12,721 --> 00:31:14,880
Boss P'Eng has some matters
he needs me to handle.

577
00:31:15,079 --> 00:31:16,200
I'll take my leave now.

578
00:31:16,373 --> 00:31:19,899
When you're finished later, the car downstairs
will safely take you back to your place.

579
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:20,839
Thanks for your hard work.

580
00:31:20,839 --> 00:31:21,839
Take care.

581
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:29,920
Phone number...

582
00:31:32,519 --> 00:31:34,078
That phone number...

583
00:31:34,079 --> 00:31:35,159
Let me think.

584
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:36,199
Let me think.

585
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:37,200
Regarding the compensation,

586
00:31:37,201 --> 00:31:38,761
I expect you to contact me proactively.

587
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,160
This is my phone number.

588
00:31:45,079 --> 00:31:46,159
Just look it up using this.

589
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:47,480
Okay.

590
00:31:52,279 --> 00:31:54,239
Your reserved room is S10.

591
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:56,015
Those guests from earlier
have already headed over.

592
00:31:56,039 --> 00:31:57,279
And you are?

593
00:31:57,759 --> 00:31:59,200
I'm...

594
00:32:00,039 --> 00:32:01,039
Their friend.

595
00:32:01,400 --> 00:32:02,400
A friend.

596
00:32:02,799 --> 00:32:03,799
Thanks.

597
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:04,839
Mm-hmm.

598
00:32:24,119 --> 00:32:25,440
What's wrong with you?

599
00:32:28,319 --> 00:32:29,319
What are you doing?

600
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:30,279
What now?

601
00:32:30,359 --> 00:32:31,400
Go to a nearby pharmacy.

602
00:32:31,799 --> 00:32:33,119
Buy a bottle of allergy medicine.

603
00:32:33,559 --> 00:32:34,559
Hurry!

604
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,239
You look like you're in pretty bad shape.

605
00:32:40,240 --> 00:32:40,880
Are you okay?

606
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:42,560
Do you need to go to the hospital?

607
00:32:44,039 --> 00:32:44,759
Hurry up.

608
00:32:45,039 --> 00:32:46,039
Cut the crap.

609
00:32:51,559 --> 00:32:52,559
What are you doing?

610
00:32:53,559 --> 00:32:54,480
Do you want me to hold your hand?

611
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:55,480
Give me the money.

612
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:57,600
How can I buy you medicine without money?

613
00:33:00,440 --> 00:33:01,440
About the money...

614
00:33:01,880 --> 00:33:02,920
I'll give it to you later.

615
00:33:03,039 --> 00:33:04,118
You said it.

616
00:33:04,119 --> 00:33:05,319
Don't try to stiff me later.

617
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:07,318
If you don't come back,

618
00:33:07,319 --> 00:33:08,680
I'll die right here.

619
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,000
Then go ahead and die.

620
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:25,559
That was close.

621
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:28,720
An unreasonable thug like you

622
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,400
deserves to die anyway.

623
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:33,320
I don't have time to play games with you.

624
00:33:35,039 --> 00:33:36,440
You're on your own. Good luck.

625
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,399
Hey, your...

626
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:57,758
your flashy boss seems to
be having an allergic reaction.

627
00:33:57,759 --> 00:33:58,759
He's in that alley.

628
00:33:59,119 --> 00:34:00,399
If you don't get over there right now,

629
00:34:00,400 --> 00:34:01,680
you'll be collecting his corpse.

630
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:20,840
This should be the place.

631
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:37,880
Just start the massage, sir.

632
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:42,640
I didn't walk into the wrong room, did I?

633
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:58,320
No, you didn't.

634
00:34:58,440 --> 00:34:59,440
That's him.

635
00:35:02,599 --> 00:35:04,400
I heard from Mr. Mingkun

636
00:35:04,880 --> 00:35:06,600
that your technique is highly professional.

637
00:35:07,079 --> 00:35:08,678
You can use a bit more force.

638
00:35:08,679 --> 00:35:09,719
I can handle the pressure.

639
00:35:11,079 --> 00:35:13,239
He thinks I'm a masseur.

640
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,159
What a golden opportunity.

641
00:35:15,840 --> 00:35:17,559
Since your boy A Pong stumbled upon this,

642
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:21,199
I'll let you taste the
power of Masseur Pong.

643
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:33,598
Let me move the towel down a bit first.

644
00:35:33,599 --> 00:35:35,038
Otherwise, I can't apply enough pressure.

645
00:35:35,039 --> 00:35:36,039
Mmhmm.

646
00:36:09,559 --> 00:36:10,839
With such a rotten temper,

647
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:12,518
you must have offended
a lot of people out there.

648
00:36:12,519 --> 00:36:13,800
Serves you right.

649
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:19,519
You...

650
00:36:19,520 --> 00:36:21,040
You really can take the pressure, huh?

651
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:22,640
I have a high pain tolerance.

652
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:24,280
You can press even harder.

653
00:36:25,920 --> 00:36:27,719
You asked for it.

654
00:36:38,400 --> 00:36:39,400
Sir,

655
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:41,199
why do you have calluses on your hands?

656
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:45,000
Oh.

657
00:36:45,360 --> 00:36:48,800
I usually lift weights and work out.

658
00:36:49,920 --> 00:36:51,080
Just staying healthy and fit.

659
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,239
And toning up while I'm at it.

660
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:57,320
Are you Tailan masseurs
this competitive nowadays?

661
00:36:57,679 --> 00:36:59,440
It's even more cutthroat than our industry.

662
00:37:00,039 --> 00:37:01,599
Your industry?

663
00:37:02,039 --> 00:37:05,119
Aren't all you bosses
chubby with beer bellies?

664
00:37:05,360 --> 00:37:06,518
You're the only one

665
00:37:06,519 --> 00:37:07,920
who's so fair and tender.

666
00:37:09,800 --> 00:37:10,879
Sir,

667
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:13,120
maybe you should use some
essential oil for the massage.

668
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:20,480
You...

669
00:37:21,039 --> 00:37:22,759
Don't tell me you forgot the essential oil.

670
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:30,679
I brought it.

671
00:37:30,880 --> 00:37:31,880
Just give me a second.

672
00:37:56,039 --> 00:37:57,439
Why is there so much for breakfast?

673
00:37:57,559 --> 00:37:59,039
Didn't I say I wanted to lose weight?

674
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:00,639
This is enough to feed a pig.

675
00:38:01,199 --> 00:38:01,599
Young Master,

676
00:38:02,039 --> 00:38:03,719
the doctor specifically advised last night

677
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:06,639
that your recent malnutrition
has lowered your immunity,

678
00:38:06,719 --> 00:38:08,296
which triggered the
severe allergic reaction.

679
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:10,960
So he suggested we must
ensure you get enough nutrients.

680
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:12,280
Preparing all this

681
00:38:12,281 --> 00:38:13,721
doesn't mean you have to eat it all.

682
00:38:14,119 --> 00:38:15,360
It's just...

683
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:18,359
it's just that your taste is like
the weather in Manchester,

684
00:38:18,360 --> 00:38:19,439
completely unpredictable.

685
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:20,320
Therefore,

686
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:21,880
please pick whatever you like.

687
00:38:22,119 --> 00:38:23,399
You've been with me for so long,

688
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:25,160
and you still don't know my taste?

689
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:26,360
I'm sorry, Young Master.

690
00:38:28,719 --> 00:38:31,079
I only know your taste in boys.

691
00:38:36,119 --> 00:38:37,879
That flower boy who ran away last night,

692
00:38:37,880 --> 00:38:38,880
did you find him?

693
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:39,679
My report, Young Master.

694
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:41,799
That Mr. Pao called last night

695
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:43,440
specifically to check on your condition.

696
00:38:43,599 --> 00:38:45,199
He must be scared out of his wits.

697
00:38:45,519 --> 00:38:48,079
Why don't we be the bigger
person and let it slide this time?

698
00:38:48,239 --> 00:38:50,279
Why lower yourself to
the level of a flower seller?

699
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:51,880
He's just feeling guilty.

700
00:38:53,039 --> 00:38:54,360
Daring to disobey my orders,

701
00:38:54,480 --> 00:38:55,639
does he have a death wish?

702
00:38:56,679 --> 00:38:57,799
If he couldn't buy it, fine.

703
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,399
But he agreed and then ran away.

704
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,920
If it were you, could you forgive him?

705
00:39:01,760 --> 00:39:02,959
If it were me,

706
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:04,320
I would have just walked away.

707
00:39:05,039 --> 00:39:06,079
Also, I double-checked.

708
00:39:06,239 --> 00:39:08,280
The alley where you were smoking last night

709
00:39:08,320 --> 00:39:11,199
was less than a hundred
meters from our car.

710
00:39:14,039 --> 00:39:15,039
I'm not eating.

711
00:39:15,199 --> 00:39:16,199
What is this garbage?

712
00:39:16,360 --> 00:39:18,200
I told you to change
the chef, but you didn't.

713
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:19,480
Young Master,

714
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:20,840
please calm down.

715
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:24,359
The one who prepared all this for you today

716
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:26,839
is the new head chef transferred
from the Mandarin Oriental.

717
00:39:26,840 --> 00:39:29,038
He's the runner-up of the Bocuse d'Or

718
00:39:29,039 --> 00:39:31,119
and took third place in the
World Golden Chef Award.

719
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:34,639
He's also the eighteenth
chef I've hired for you.

720
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,360
What's the point of all those awards?

721
00:39:36,679 --> 00:39:38,439
I don't like this
flashy, impractical stuff.

722
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:40,480
I want food meant for humans.

723
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,320
Food for humans, do you understand?

724
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:45,959
It seems you still prefer

725
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:48,239
the home-cooked meals
Madam used to make for you.

726
00:39:49,159 --> 00:39:50,159
Right?

727
00:39:53,159 --> 00:39:54,159
I can't eat them anymore.

728
00:39:54,559 --> 00:39:56,679
Anyway, hurry up and find
someone who suits my taste.

729
00:39:57,320 --> 00:39:58,799
And that boy from last night,

730
00:39:58,800 --> 00:40:00,400
I must see him today.

731
00:40:01,199 --> 00:40:02,519
I want him

732
00:40:03,039 --> 00:40:04,039
dead.

733
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:11,799
Hey, I'm talking to you.

734
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:12,800
Did you hear me?

735
00:40:12,960 --> 00:40:14,960
Come here and report
directly to the Young Master.

736
00:40:17,519 --> 00:40:19,239
Reporting, Young Master, I heard you.

737
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:20,759
I'll arrange for the stable hands later

738
00:40:20,760 --> 00:40:22,639
to bring out all five of our horses.

739
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:23,960
Bring them out for what?

740
00:40:24,199 --> 00:40:25,879
Did I say I wanted to go horseback riding?

741
00:40:27,119 --> 00:40:28,158
No, Young Master.

742
00:40:28,159 --> 00:40:29,279
They're not for you to ride.

743
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:30,800
They're prepared for that boy.

744
00:40:31,039 --> 00:40:31,800
Once we find him,

745
00:40:31,880 --> 00:40:34,135
we'll have him drawn and quartered
by five horses, just as you ordered.

746
00:40:34,159 --> 00:40:35,239
You can rest assured.

747
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:39,495
Reporting to the Young Master,

748
00:40:39,519 --> 00:40:41,000
I have something to report.

749
00:40:41,239 --> 00:40:42,239
Speak.

750
00:40:42,960 --> 00:40:43,960
Madam's...

751
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,920
The diamond ring Madam left behind

752
00:40:46,760 --> 00:40:47,639
is missing.

753
00:40:47,640 --> 00:40:49,119
Missing?

754
00:40:50,719 --> 00:40:52,280
Wasn't it in the safe in the study?

755
00:40:52,320 --> 00:40:53,199
How could it be missing?

756
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:54,400
It was probably...

757
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,919
It was probably taken by
Gardener Pao, who tends the garden.

758
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:58,959
The security footage shows she was
the only one who entered the study.

759
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,719
And she also has a key.

760
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:03,158
Why would the gardener have a key?

761
00:41:03,159 --> 00:41:05,800
We don't know that either.

762
00:41:07,440 --> 00:41:08,598
Do you know Auntie Pao's whereabouts?

763
00:41:08,599 --> 00:41:09,719
Or her home address?

764
00:41:10,159 --> 00:41:11,679
Yes, we do.

765
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:14,718
Young Master, the top priority right now

766
00:41:14,719 --> 00:41:16,400
is to find Madam's ring first.

767
00:41:16,760 --> 00:41:18,479
I'll arrange for someone to look for it.

768
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:19,480
Just wait for my news.

769
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:22,118
It must be that jinx from
last night haunting me,

770
00:41:22,119 --> 00:41:23,960
bringing all this bad luck.

771
00:41:26,039 --> 00:41:26,679
Come with me.

772
00:41:26,679 --> 00:41:27,280
Young Master!

773
00:41:27,280 --> 00:41:28,280
Young...
